  {"i":4154,"t":["actions","festivals"],"n":"Decorating is taught mainly with festivals (New Year, Tanabata); the link to home is too loose for a third unit."},
  {"i":4169,"t":["qualities","school"],"n":"試験の範囲 is the context learners meet most, so school is a real second unit."},
  {"i":4235,"t":["movement"],"n":"Drifting and wafting make this a general movement verb; nature is only an association."},
  {"i":4237,"t":["qualities"],"n":"It is a descriptive adjective (personal/private), not a word about people as a topic."},
  {"i":4247,"t":["travel","culture","city"],"n":"Castles are taught first as sightseeing spots and heritage; the town-places unit comes after."},
  {"i":4267,"t":["character","qualities"],"s":{"4":["function"]},"n":"Senses 1-2 describe careless character. Sense 4 (いい加減疲れた) is a degree adverb that N3 learners meet."},
  {"i":4289,"t":["actions"],"n":"Peeking is an everyday action; a body unit would not teach it."},
  {"i":4299,"t":["thinking"],"s":{"3":["culture"]},"n":"Realizing and perceiving belong to thinking. Buddhist enlightenment (悟りを開く) is a known sense that belongs to religion."}
